WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.610
Every time a Latin American government tries
to discuss foreign policy and development,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.860
they end up discussing regional integration...

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.680
That is why we should understand the three
main common features of Latin America: football

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.150
(soccer for you Americans), revolutions and…
the regional organisations.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.730
Seriously, we're not kidding:

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:31.400
In the last few decades there have been so
many regional organisations that it is almost

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.190
impossible to know what goals each of them
have, besides, obviously, being an excuse

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:40.250
for spending money on public workers, headquarters,
and travelling...

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:45.910
UNASUR, MERCOSUR, ALBA, CARICOM, CELAC, ALADI,
the Andean Community, SICA, SELA, the Rio

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:48.710
Group, and of course the Organization of American
States…

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.920
And, the truth is, I’m sure I’ve not even
mentioned all of them…

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:58.100
Anyway, once we know about all these organisations
we could think that Latin America is the place

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.800
where people get on with each other best,
a place where it’s easy to do business among

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.399
the different countries, and where governments
work together for the common good, right?

00:01:08.399 --> 00:01:09.399
Right!?

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:13.700
Well, bad news, none of that is true…

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:19.150
All these organisations were born with high
ideas, but we could say they all really did

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:23.520
nothing for development and economic and political
integration.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.170
(“In Latin America new institutions are
created, but it isn't clear what to do with

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.340
the previous ones.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.310
It is an endless flight forward”.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.409
Carlos Malamud)

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:37.370
Look, despite all the different processes
of integration, trade is strangely low among

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.280
the different countries.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:44.780
The numbers are important here: the share
of exports inside the region hasn’t changed

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:49.420
much, it has been around 20%, much lower than
other parts of the world.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:59.950
This is pretty strong evidence about how artificial
and unproductive these organisations are.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.910
We will see the details of this case, though
the word disappointment or failure would probably

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.619
better describe Mercosur.

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:09.869
But I can already tell you it is very possible
that this lack of real integration is the

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:17.209
origin of some of the most important problems
that the region is facing.

00:02:17.209 --> 00:02:20.239
THE ETERNAL PROMISE

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:22.959
Latin America is, dear viewers, a fantastic
region.

00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:27.980
It’s got great natural resources, it has
significant biodiversity, and its climate

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.480
is varied and impressive.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:35.370
Many people would say that the region is one
of the most beautiful on earth.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:42.639
However…economically speaking, things are
not looking so great.

00:02:42.639 --> 00:02:47.309
Despite all these magnificent resources and
its great potential, the region has been left

00:02:47.309 --> 00:02:49.199
behind in terms of economic growth.

00:02:49.199 --> 00:02:54.079
Let´s compare, for example, the current richest
country in Latin America: Chile.

00:02:54.079 --> 00:02:59.469
So, I think most would agree that Chile has
done a good job in the last few decades, right?

00:02:59.469 --> 00:03:03.669
Well, despite that apparent progress, just
have a look at this chart...

00:03:03.669 --> 00:03:15.739
Now here, we have taken the richest country
in Latin America and we have compared it to

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:19.400
South Korea, which is not the richest in Eastern
Asia.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.510
And, well, the difference is quite obvious.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:26.989
In the 60s, Chile was a poor country, but
far richer than South Korea...

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:36.169
Today, well, things they are rather different.

00:03:36.169 --> 00:03:40.120
We could also look at Argentina, which once
was the richest country in Latin America (with

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.809
the exception of Cuba).

00:03:41.809 --> 00:03:49.370
Now take a look at its evolution when compared
to Spain.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:55.749
Well, one of the causes of this lower growth
might be precisely the low trade integration

00:03:55.749 --> 00:04:00.780
and the excess protectionism and bureaucracy
that the region has always suffered from.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:05.849
Something like: lots of agreements, committees
and forums…but, when the rubber hits the

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:08.379
road, there’s really nothing there.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:10.919
But, hold on for just a second…

00:04:10.919 --> 00:04:14.859
A few years ago a new integration project
was put in place...

00:04:14.859 --> 00:04:18.859
And this one is actually completely different
to the rest.

00:04:18.859 --> 00:04:23.669
Not only is this the first project with real
success in the region, it might also change

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:26.139
the destiny of Latin America forever.

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:35.669
We are talking about the Pacific Alliance.

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:39.449
THE PACIFIC ALLIANCE

00:04:39.449 --> 00:04:44.620
In April 2011, our friends, Chile, Colombia,
Mexico and Peru formed the so-called Pacific

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.620
Alliance.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:50.139
Its mission is to finally achieve an integration
so that goods, capital, and people could move

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:51.979
freely around the region.

00:04:51.979 --> 00:04:56.259
All this was put in place with the idea that
it would stimulate growth, development and

00:04:56.259 --> 00:04:59.380
competitiveness in these economies.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:04.199
"Our countries account for 55 percent of Latin
American exports…

00:05:04.199 --> 00:05:06.810
This is not a romantic integration, a poetic
integration.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:10.759
It is a realistic integration before the world
and to the world.

00:05:10.759 --> 00:05:14.069
». Alan García, former President of Peru.

00:05:14.069 --> 00:05:15.570
And so they did.

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:21.550
Even though there is still a lot to be done,
since then, development has been… how to

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.069
put it… well, significant.

00:05:24.069 --> 00:05:30.530
In only 6 years, these four countries have
removed 92% of the customs tariffs and they

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.139
have set a deadline to remove the rest of
them as well.

00:05:33.139 --> 00:05:36.900
Along with this, they have simplified the
bureaucracy of customs and administration.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.180
Especially when it comes to rules about the
origin of goods.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.879
which was previously a significant burden
on the region.

00:05:43.879 --> 00:05:50.591
So, up until now, if a Colombian producer
used Peruvian suppliers, he couldn’t take

00:05:50.591 --> 00:05:55.610
advantage of the free trade agreement between
Colombia and Mexico when selling his goods

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:56.610
to Mexico.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.659
It was crazy.

00:05:58.659 --> 00:06:01.580
But that is not the end of it.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:06.949
Visa requirements have also been eliminated,
so the movement of visitors has doubled.

00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:12.379
And then, and this is very important, there
have been significant advances in financial

00:06:12.379 --> 00:06:13.379
integration.

00:06:13.379 --> 00:06:18.660
These four countries have created the MILA,
the American Integrated Market, which is meant

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.710
to be the largest stock market in Latin America...

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:28.960
And there´s more: among other initiatives,
the countries in the alliance are working

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.020
together in order to be known in international
markets.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:35.909
They have also started to share embassies
in African and Asian countries, and they have

00:06:35.909 --> 00:06:39.840
decided to negotiate all together their free
trade agreements.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:43.569
For example, they have already started to
do this with New Zealand, Australia, Canada

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.360
and Singapore.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.620
“Australia and New Zealand Start Trade Talks
With Pacific Alliance”.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:49.620
Wall Street Journal.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:54.460
In other words, these four countries are building,
step by step, a unique market which will be

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:55.939
rather significant.

00:06:55.939 --> 00:07:00.900
We are talking about more than 214 million
consumers here with a combined GDP which makes

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:08.550
this alliance one of the 8 largest economies
in the world.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:13.960
This is an economy that represents 50% of
all exports and more than 40% of all foreign

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.150
investment in Latin America.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:20.479
We could say that, if the Pacific Alliance
keeps it up, in a very short time, we might

00:07:20.479 --> 00:07:23.639
have to consider it the biggest power in Latin
America...

00:07:23.639 --> 00:07:28.090
But, in order to understand a bit better the
achievements they have had in only 6 years,

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:31.039
we should look at the other large group in
the region: MERCOSUR.

00:07:31.039 --> 00:07:36.240
THE DOWNFALL OF MERCOSUR?

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:44.169
MERCOSUR was created in 1991 by Brazil, Argentina,
Uruguay and Paraguay with the intention of

00:07:44.169 --> 00:07:47.200
creating one large integrated market.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:52.050
Well, these were ambitious goals... but the
advances have been much more modest.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:54.050
So, how about some evidence of this…

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:55.250
Well, look:

00:07:55.250 --> 00:08:00.370
The trade among Mercosur members represents
today less than 13% of the total trade of

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.770
its members.

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.860
In 1995 it was almost 20%.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:11.669
So, rather than encouraging trade between
its members, we could say MERCOSUR has weakened

00:08:11.669 --> 00:08:12.669
them.

00:08:12.669 --> 00:08:17.169
In the last few years, MERCOSUR has become
some sort of protectionist shield rather than

00:08:17.169 --> 00:08:22.159
something which is working to integrate these
countries.

00:08:22.159 --> 00:08:26.969
“The group has become little more than an
anti-gringo talking shop”.

00:08:26.969 --> 00:08:27.969
Financial Times, 2013.

00:08:27.969 --> 00:08:29.819
But, why isn’t it working?

00:08:29.819 --> 00:08:33.930
Well, mainly because there is no commitment.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:38.539
In theory, MERCOSUR is a process of economic
integration but there are so many exceptions

00:08:38.539 --> 00:08:43.070
and restrictions that, in the end, there is
no free movement of goods or services.

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:46.490
MERCOSUR has become an something which is
totally ineffective…

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:51.060
Look, a good example can be found on the border
between Argentina and Uruguay.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.870
In theory, the goods should be able to move
freely between both countries.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:59.490
However, the reality is very different: when
adding customs, inspections and bureaucracy,

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:07.970
a truck from Uruguay to Argentina could be
delayed more than 24 hours…

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:10.290
Crazy.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:15.680
All of this has made Uruguay formally ask
to become a member of the Pacific Alliance.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:20.910
And there is more, the political change in
Argentina and Brazil has led to both of their

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:27.040
governments accepting that MERCOSUR, at least
as it is understood today, is almost completely

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.050
worthless.

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:32.800
“We’ll never reach the common market,
the custom union is completely destroyed and

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.740
the free trade area is not working either.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.430
MERCOSUR is in a dying state”.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:40.460
Danilo Astori, Minister of Economy in Uruguay.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:45.269
That is why Macri has decided to become closer
to the Pacific Alliance and look for ties

00:09:45.269 --> 00:09:47.589
between both processes of integration.

00:09:47.589 --> 00:09:51.730
The question is: Will the Pacific Alliance
create a change in MERCOSUR?

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:59.350
If it does that would be great news for the
whole region.

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:00.850
THE PACIFIC PUMAS

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:11.210
Well, now we have to ask: Why is the Pacific
Alliance, unlike the rest of organisations,

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.390
the only one that seems to be working?

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:19.550
Maybe it has to do with the so-called Pacific
Pumas: Chile, Peru, Colombia and Mexico.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:24.160
These countries have been the most dynamic
economies in Latin America, and they share

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:25.170
the same vision…

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:29.160
They all agree: in order to grow and develop,
they have to produce and do business with

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.280
the rest of the world.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:34.810
And this is why, according to the World Bank,
these pumas are the countries where it is

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:38.820
easiest to do business, or where more trade
agreements are signed with the rest of the

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:43.880
world.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:52.540
Anyway, the Pacific Alliance represents one
of the best opportunities for Latin America

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.700
to be in a position to become the talk of
the town.

00:10:55.700 --> 00:11:00.810
We might even be witnessing the birth of a
great economic power...

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:05.910
But now it is your turn: Do you think Latin
America has to bet on these processes of integration?

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:09.550
Leave your opinion on the comments below as
well as in this quick poll.

